<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-cyanobacteria-mat-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Cyanobacteria mat Turing ocellus wavelength at 64.19 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Cyanobacteria mat (Stromatolite Mat))",
        "Cyanobacteria mat Turing ocellus wavelength at 64.19 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Cyanobacteria mat (Stromatolite Mat) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-cyanobacteria-mat-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-cyanobacteria-mat-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-cyanobacteria-mat-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-cyanobacteria-mat-turing-wavelength-s0-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-cyanobacteria-mat-turing-wavelength-s0-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-cyanobacteria-mat-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Cyanobacteria mat (Stromatolite Mat) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-cyanobacteria-mat-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Cyanobacteria mat (Stromatolite Mat)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That Petroff's cone equation is being integrated",
        "does_not_claim: That a paper measured 64.19 µm as a pigment wavelength of this mat",
        "does_not_claim: That colony-size distributions match the spots (KS = 0.453)",
        "does_not_claim: That the plate photograph is a 64 µm micrograph",
        "reconstructed_in_script: A display transfer that paints activator peaks as beige colonies on illuminated agar for comparison with the culture plate",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Diffusivities, including the measured finite-amplitude factor 1.08, so the saturated Fourier mode is 64.19 µm",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Eigenvector single-mode growth rates, equal-diffusion ablation, and the diffusivity sweep",
        "reported_in_source: Petroff et al. 2010 centimetre-scale conical stromatolite spacing",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics",
        "reported_in_source: Shepard and Sumner 2010 reticulate mats from filament motility",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the existence of a selected finite wavenumber",
        "transfer_boundary: The culture plate is macroscopic. Morphometrics that compare it to the 513.5 µm domain are scale-free (CV spectra, median-normalised diameters)." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-cyanobacteria-mat-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/cyanobacteria_mat_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Cyanobacteria mat (Stromatolite Mat); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the existence of a selected finite wavenumber | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics | Petroff et al. 2010 centimetre-scale conical stromatolite spacing | Shepard and Sumner 2010 reticulate mats from filament motility; reconstructed_in_script: Diffusivities, including the measured finite-amplitude factor 1.08, so the saturated Fourier mode is 64.19 µm | Eigenvector single-mode growth rates, equal-diffusion ablation, and the diffusivity sweep | A display transfer that paints activator peaks as beige colonies on illuminated agar for comparison with the culture plate; transfer_boundary: The culture plate is macroscopic. Morphometrics that compare it to the 513.5 µm domain are scale-free (CV spectra, median-normalised diameters).; does_not_claim: That a paper measured 64.19 µm as a pigment wavelength of this mat | That the plate photograph is a 64 µm micrograph | That colony-size distributions match the spots (KS = 0.453) | That Petroff's cone equation is being integrated]; phenomenon_size: 9.0 cm (0.09 m, log10=-1.046 m, tier=7_organism_cm); species_scale_ladder (1 runs from 9.0 cm to 9.0 cm): 9.0 cm:petroff-stromatolite" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1001973107>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1472-4669.2010.00235.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1128/AEM.00819-08> ;
