        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-cyanobacteria-mat-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cyanobacteria-mat-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cyanobacteria mat Turing ocellus wavelength at 64.19 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 85.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Schnakenberg Turing system on a periodic 8-wavelength domain for a Holocene cyanobacteria mat (chronoseries 1/1, age 0 Ma, tier 4_cellular_10um). The saturated activator locks to the Fourier shell at 64.19 µm. Eigenvector growth rates match analytical sigma(k) with Pearson r = 0.999986 and RMSE = 0.00558. A bin-mean estimator on the same run scores r = 0.529 and is retained as a negative control. Equal diffusion decays (sigma_max = -0.059). The diffusivity sweep correlates with sqrt(gamma) at r = 0.9995. The culture plate (137 colonies, area CV 1.642) is not the same size distribution as the spots (65 peaks, area CV 0.295, KS = 0.453). GIF versus plate cv_sim_similarity = 90.7. Overall 85.6. Overall 85.6/100 (faithfulness 84.9, reproducibility 87.2); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8c1db788ac0382399c6119652ec88de045be6725; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 85, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/cyanobacteria_mat_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-cyanobacteria-mat-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 8c1db788ac0382399c6119652ec88de045be6725, image/png, 619956 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 29d2a0dd6b33420d9440717158f41c52cdeec9d201133dce28106873830495dc (sha256 29d2a0dd6b33420d9440717158f41c52cdeec9d201133dce28106873830495dc), spec_fingerprint 17c14d868777fb5a50af2e088b23ad6bf8798c31500d2ec6dec6508dc89f427c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 17c14d868777fb5a50af2e088b23ad6bf8798c31500d2ec6dec6508dc89f427c; artifact_sha256: 29d2a0dd6b33420d9440717158f41c52cdeec9d201133dce28106873830495dc; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/cyanobacteria_mat_turing_wavelength_s0/cyanobacteria_mat_holocene_culture_plate.jpg=858930a5ad520ee4..., datasets/cyanobacteria_mat_turing_wavelength_s0/cyanobacteria_mat_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=d166e23ba481aac8...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the existence of a selected finite wavenumber | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics | Petroff et al. 2010 centimetre-scale conical stromatolite spacing | Shepard and Sumner 2010 reticulate mats from filament motility; reconstructed_in_script: Diffusivities, including the measured finite-amplitude factor 1.08, so the saturated Fourier mode is 64.19 µm | Eigenvector single-mode growth rates, equal-diffusion ablation, and the diffusivity sweep | A display transfer that paints activator peaks as beige colonies on illuminated agar for comparison with the culture plate; transfer_boundary: The culture plate is macroscopic. Morphometrics that compare it to the 513.5 µm domain are scale-free (CV spectra, median-normalised diameters).; does_not_claim: That a paper measured 64.19 µm as a pigment wavelength of this mat | That the plate photograph is a 64 µm micrograph | That colony-size distributions match the spots (KS = 0.453) | That Petroff's cone equation is being integrated." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Integer-shell sweep collapsed gamma=1.5 and gamma=2.0 onto one mode (r=0.967). Replace the sweep summary with the narrow-band power-weighted wavelength.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Keep an equal-diffusion ablation with sigma_max < 0 and a decaying RMS ratio, and print it on the comparison figure.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Segment the real culture plate and compare median-normalised diameters to activator peaks with a KS statistic. Do not copy a simulation scalar into the specimen column.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Replace the broadband bin-mean dispersion fit (r=0.529) with eigenvector-initialised single-mode growth, and keep the rejected r as a measured control.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.56e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cyanobacteria-mat-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cyanobacteria mat Turing ocellus wavelength at 64.19 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 88/100" ;
